/**
 * Marrakech Eco Tours — post-tour quality form.
 * Generated for 48 tours. Internal quality tracking; nothing is published.
 *
 * WHY THE CLIENT NEVER SCROLLS 48 TOURS
 * -------------------------------------
 * Two paths, both built by this script:
 *
 *  1. THE LINK YOU SEND. makeLinks() prints one link per tour with the tour
 *     already filled in. The client lands straight on the questions. This is
 *     the path you will use every time.
 *
 *  2. THE PICKER, for when someone opens the bare form. Google Forms cannot
 *     filter a list live — every question is fixed when the form is built —
 *     but an answer CAN jump to a different page. So the narrowing is real,
 *     built out of pages:
 *
 *         kind of trip?  ->  how long?  ->  a list of 1-7 tours
 *
 *     27 leaf pages, most holding three tours or fewer. Three taps, no
 *     scrolling.
 *
 * SETUP
 *   1. script.google.com -> New project
 *   2. Paste this whole file, replacing the default myFunction
 *   3. Run -> createForm    (approve the permission prompt once)
 *   4. Run -> makeLinks     then View -> Executions/Logs to copy the links
 *
 * Re-running createForm builds a BRAND NEW form and leaves the old one
 * untouched. If you have hand-edited questions in the Forms UI, re-running
 * will not carry those edits across.
 *
 * Verified against the Apps Script Forms reference (Sept 2026): prefilling is
 * FormResponse.toPrefilledUrl(), branching is Choice navigation, and choice
 * navigation overrules a page's own setGoToPage.
 */

